# The Reports page's job families: which scheduled jobs share a lamp.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/report-families.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the lines below
# are examples. Job names are your own, so the real list stays outside the
# checkout. Without a report-families.conf the page draws no family lamp, lists
# every job under "Other jobs", and says why.
#
# Pipe-separated, one family per line, in the order the page draws them:
#
#   family|<key>|<label>|<icon>|<job>,<job>,...
#
# <key> and <icon> are lower-case words joined by hyphens; <icon> names an icon
# in the dashboard's set (for example hard-drive-download, git-compare,
# heart-pulse, bot, book-open). A job belongs to one family at most; a job no
# family names is listed under "Other jobs". A line the page cannot read is
# named on the page and skipped.

family|backups|Backups|hard-drive-download|db-backup-nightly,offsite-verify
family|repos|Repos & setup|git-compare|repo-sync-nightly,brew-doctor-nightly
family|host|Host health|heart-pulse|health-check-nightly,watchdog-daily
family|agents|Agent routines|bot|morning-brief,weekly-digest
